{title: Holy God, We Praise Thy Name}
{artist: Ignaz Franz · tr. Clarence Walworth}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
[F]Holy God, we [Bb]praise thy [C]name; [F]Lord of [Bb]all, we [C]bow be[F]fore thee!
All on earth thy [Bb]scepter [C]claim, [F]all in [Bb]heaven a[C]bove a[F]dore thee;
[C]infinite thy [F]vast do[C]main, [F]ever[Bb]last[C]ing [F]is thy reign.

Verse 2
Hark! the loud
celestial hymn Angel choirs above
are raising, Cherubim
and seraphim, In
unceasing chorus praising;
Fill the
heavens with sweet
accord: Holy, holy, holy, Lord.

Verse 3
Lo! the apostolic train
Join the sacred Name
to hallow; Prophets swell
the loud
refrain, And the white
robed martyrs follow;
And from
morn to set
of sun, Through
the Church
the song
goes on.

Verse 4
Holy Father, Holy Son,
Holy Spirit, Three
we name Thee;
While in essence only One,
Undivided God
we claim Thee;
And adoring bend
the knee, While
we own
the mystery.
